2. GROUP BY and HAVING :-GROUP BY is used to group rows having the same value so that we can apply aggregate functions like count,sum,average,max and min
HAVING is used to filter the groups created by GROUP BY

1. Find the number of employees in each department
   SELECT department, COUNT(*) FROM employee GROUP BY department;

2. Find the average salary of each department
   SELECT department, avg(sal) from employee group by department;

3. Find departments having more than 5 employees
   SELECT department, COUNT(*) FROM employee GROUP BY department HAVING COUNT(*) > 5;

