31. Query optimization
    Query optimization is the process of improving a SQL query so that it executes faster and uses fewer database resources.

    First, I use EXPLAIN / execution plan to understand how the database is executing the query. Then I check whether appropriate indexes are being used, whether there are inefficient joins, and whether a full table scan can be avoided. I select only the required columns instead of using SELECT *. I also check for N+1 query problems at the application/JPA level and use pagination when retrieving large amounts of data.

    Query Optimization
       ↓
1. EXPLAIN / Execution Plan
       ↓
2. Check Indexes
       ↓
3. Check Joins
       ↓
4. Avoid unnecessary Full Table Scans
       ↓
5. Select required columns
       ↓
6. Avoid N+1 queries
       ↓
7. Use Pagination for large results

