1. Serial GC

Uses a single thread for garbage collection.

Stops application threads while collecting.

Suitable for small applications with limited memory.

JVM option: -XX:+UseSerialGC

2. Parallel GC

Uses multiple threads for garbage collection.

Focuses on high application throughput.

Can cause noticeable pauses during collection.

JVM option: -XX:+UseParallelGC

3. G1 GC (Garbage-First)

Divides the heap into regions.

Prioritizes regions expected to yield more reclaimable memory.

Tries to meet a configurable pause-time goal.

JVM option: -XX:+UseG1GC

4. ZGC

Designed for very low pause times.

Performs most expensive GC work concurrently with application execution.

Useful for applications with large heaps and strict latency requirements.

JVM option: -XX:+UseZGC


